window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["0e"]={"https://theconversation.com/its-possible-to-predict-some-el-ninos-a-year-in-advance-heres-why-that-matters-295063":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"3869a994c00b1b1a4444a42438caabaf04f77f07fe8fb0fd3fda2f2a56a75138","read":"https://theconversation.com/its-possible-to-predict-some-el-ninos-a-year-in-advance-heres-why-that-matters-295063","bytes":182823,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"It’s possible to predict some El Niños a year in advance. Here’s why that matters","by":[{"n":"Nandini Ramesh","r":"Senior Research Scientist, CSIRO"},{"n":"Mandy Freund","r":"Lecturer, Climate Science Geography, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-09T18:42:17Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A remarkably strong El Niño ",["has formed","https://wmo.int/news/media-centre/el-nino-set-become-very-strong-raising-risks-of-extreme-weather-2027"]," in the Pacific."]},{"k":"p","s":["This natural ",["phenomenon","https://theconversation.com/a-record-shattering-el-nino-is-almost-here-heres-what-that-means-for-the-worlds-weather-291258"]," drives variations in temperature, rainfall and winds across the globe. The ongoing El Niño has already contributed to ",["sudden floods","https://www.undp.org/africa/resilience-hub-africa/blog/drought-deluge-preparing-eastern-africa-el-ninos-double-hit"]," in eastern Africa, ",["blistering heatwaves","https://e360.yale.edu/digest/el-nino-2026"]," in Europe and ",["intense hurricanes","https://www.bbc.com/weather/articles/c6dx07dznpyyo"]," in the eastern Pacific."]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia’s ",["Bureau of Meteorology","https://www.bom.gov.au/climate/enso/wrap-up/archive/20260616.archive.shtml"]," warned us of this El Niño in June, which is currently the earliest point at which reliable predictions can be made."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our ",["new study","https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.aeg8654"]," suggests it may be possible to accurately predict some El Niños up to 12 months ahead of time, buying valuable time for farmers, emergency services and disaster-prone communities."]},{"k":"h","s":["How models predict El Niño and La Niña"]},{"k":"p","s":["Climate and weather forecasting largely relies on physics-based models of the Earth’s atmosphere and oceans. These models work by applying the laws of physics, such as Newton’s laws of motion, to Earth’s geography."]},{"k":"p","s":["A model is given information like the shapes of continents, the locations of mountains and the speed of Earth’s rotation. The models then solve equations representing the laws of physics to simulate a version of our Earth, complete with its own storms, ocean currents, waves and wind patterns."]},{"k":"p","s":["To make predictions of El Niños and La Niñas, forecasters supply these models with information about present conditions, including ocean temperatures, currents, winds and humidity. This data comes from a vast global network of ",["satellites","https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/earth-observation-data-basics"],", ",["weather stations","https://climatedataguide.ucar.edu/climate-data/hadisd-sub-daily-non-interpolated-weather-station-data"],", ",["ocean buoys","https://climatedataguide.ucar.edu/climate-data/argo-ocean-temperature-and-salinity-profiles"]," and ",["moorings","https://climatedataguide.ucar.edu/climate-data/tropical-moored-buoy-system-tao-triton-pirata-rama-toga"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The models use this information about the present as a starting point. They then simulate the ocean and atmosphere’s movements and temperatures a few months into the future, showing whether an El Niño or La Niña is about to emerge."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why is it difficult to make early forecasts?"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the 1960s, meteorologist ",["Ed Lorenz","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Norton_Lorenz#Chaos_theory"]," and computer scientist ",["Margaret Hamilton","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Hamilton_(software_engineer)"]," made a startling discovery. Using an early weather model, they found changing the starting conditions by a tiny amount, such as a millionth of a degree Celsius, could radically alter the model’s predictions."]},{"k":"p","s":["This spawned the mathematical field of ",["chaos theory","https://vimeo.com/287523707"],", the idea that no matter how perfect a model is, there are some situations where the system being predicted is so sensitive to minuscule changes, it’s almost impossible to make correct predictions. This makes it extremely difficult to form accurate forecasts of weather more than a week or two in advance."]},{"k":"p","s":["El Niños and La Niñas are largely shaped by the ocean, which moves much more slowly and takes longer to heat up and cool down, compared to the atmosphere. As a result, El Niño and La Niña predictions can be made over a longer period. These events typically peak ",["around December","https://www.bbc.com/weather/articles/cmlye0d7q7zno"]," and can be accurately predicted about six months ahead."]},{"k":"p","s":["But these predictions also have limits. Forecasts made between ",["March and May","https://theconversation.com/the-flap-of-a-butterflys-wings-why-autumn-is-not-a-good-time-to-predict-if-el-nino-is-coming-201940"]," are notoriously unreliable. Because of the conditions in the atmosphere and ocean at this time of year, it becomes susceptible to the butterfly effect, with even small fluctuations preventing models from making accurate predictions. This period is like a Bermuda triangle for climate forecasting."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["A record-shattering El Niño is almost here. Here’s what that means for the world’s weather","https://theconversation.com/a-record-shattering-el-nino-is-almost-here-heres-what-that-means-for-the-worlds-weather-291258"]]},{"k":"h","s":["What we studied"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our ",["latest study","https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.aeg8654"]," examined whether it’s possible to overcome this uncertainty to reliably predict future El Niños."]},{"k":"p","s":["Chaotic systems are not unpredictable all the time. Sometimes the conditions are right for good predictions. A ",["few studies","https://doi.org/10.1002/2017GL074904"]," of particular years suggest some El Niño and La Niña events might be accurately predicted before the March-May period."]},{"k":"p","s":["But our research team wanted to know for sure if we should believe early forecasts. To do this, we used a massive dataset of 7,500 forecasts generated by nine models, developed in different countries. By analysing this data, we were able to check whether early predictions came true and search for patterns in early forecast performance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our findings suggest the conditions in which a forecast is made has a significant effect on its accuracy. We sorted forecasts based on what was happening in the Pacific when they were first initiated – La Niña, El Niño or neutral conditions."]},{"k":"p","s":["A clear pattern emerged: forecasts that began during a La Niña were most successful in predicting what would happen a year later. By contrast, forecasts initiated in neutral conditions were very likely to be wrong."]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings were consistent across all nine models we studied. This suggests La Niña conditions have a stabilising influence, meaning predictions are more likely to be reliable."]},{"k":"h","s":["What next?"]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings are valuable for communities worldwide. During La Niña years, we have an opportunity to make early forecasts and issue early warnings so communities, emergency responders and governments can prepare for future El Niños."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, we need more research to translate these findings into practice. Studies should focus on why La Niña events support better model performance and if there are particular ocean or atmosphere patterns that can tell us when a model is making correct predictions. Research should also investigate how best to apply these findings to interpreting real-time forecasts."]},{"k":"p","s":["This information will allow scientists to distinguish between unreliable predictions and those that might protect communities from harm."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Extreme El Niños are coming. Reaching net zero sooner means facing fewer of them","https://theconversation.com/extreme-el-ninos-are-coming-reaching-net-zero-sooner-means-facing-fewer-of-them-292134"]]}],"chars":5382},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"0391db8777bc0bf492d32c4612adb7ef27add34b7a0d200bd0557a6a94b1ee34","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/armenia","bytes":51933,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Armenia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-01T17:29:01+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Armenia-Azerbaijan border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border with Azerbaijan remains closed. FCDO advises against all travel to within 5km of the entire eastern border between Armenia and Azerbaijan, due to tensions between the 2 countries."]},{"k":"hs","s":["M16/H26 road between Ijevan and Noyemberyan"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel along the M16/H26 road between the towns of Ijevan and Noyemberyan, due to border tensions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Armenia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Armenia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Armenian Embassy in the UK","https://www.mfa.am/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entering Armenia across the land border from Iran"]},{"k":"p","s":["Armenia-Iran border is open to foreign nationals coming from Iran. This is subject to change at short notice. If you decide to leave Iran, you do so at your own risk and the British government cannot do anything to ensure your safety. Only travel if you feel it is safe to do so. In Iran, holding a British passport or having perceived connections to the UK can be reason enough for the Iranian authorities to detain you."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals entering Armenia from Iran will need a valid passport, see ‘ ",["passport validity requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia/entry-requirements"],"’. You do not need a visa to enter Armenia, see ‘ ",["visa requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia/entry-requirements"],"’."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more FCDO advice ",["if you’re affected by a crisis abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Armenia, your passport must be valid for the duration of your stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Armenia without a visa for up to 180 days in a year for tourism or business."]},{"k":"p","s":["To extend your stay, contact the Administration Department for Passports and Visas (OVIR)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Address: Davtashen, 4th District, 31/2 Building, Yerevan, Armenia 0054"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: +374 11 36 1394, +374 11 36 9140"]},{"k":"p","s":["To work or study, you must check the requirements from the ",["Armenian Embassy in the UK","https://www.mfa.am/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Armenia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/12/armenia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Armenia. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Armenia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Armenia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Armenia, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although a ceasefire exists, the eastern border between Armenia and Azerbaijan is closed and tensions remain. See ",["regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia/regional-risks"]," for details about FCDO’s warning against all travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests sometimes take place in central Yerevan and other major cities. These are usually organised by opposition political parties or activist groups highlighting topical social and political issues. Although protests tend to be peaceful and usually pass off without incident, avoid large crowds and demonstrations, follow the advice and instructions of the local authorities, monitor the media and remain vigilant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low. There are occasional incidents of pickpocketing, bag-snatching, theft from cars and burglary involving foreign nationals. To help protect your belongings:"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave spare cash, passports and valuables in a safe place"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry a copy of the photo page of your passport rather than the original document"]},{"k":"li","s":["when using ATMs check no one is watching or following you"]},{"k":"li","s":["take particular care if using an ATM after dark"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you possess, use or smuggle illegal drugs, including cannabis, you can get heavy fines and a long jail sentence, including when transiting through the airport. The penalty for smuggling drugs is a prison sentence of between 4 and 10 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to use, possess or trade marijuana, cannabidiol (CBD), or tetrahydrocannabinol (THC) products. You can be prosecuted for having these substances even when they are prescribed for medical purposes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Armenia have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and binoculars in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to photograph sites such as military bases, equipment and installations. These are considered sensitive areas and visitors have been detained and questioned for attempting to photograph them."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity has been legal since 2003 but many Armenians still view same-sex couples with disapproval. LGBT+ people in Armenia tend to be discreet about their sexuality. Local LGBT+ groups occasionally suffer from verbal and physical harassment. Physical contact between members of the same sex, such as holding hands and kissing, are common signs of friendship in Armenian culture, and not necessarily an indicator of sexual orientation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Disorderly behaviour"]},{"k":"p","s":["Armenian society does not tolerate drinking to excess as this leads to disorderly behaviour, particularly during the late evening and through the night. British nationals have been arrested for drunken behaviour."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you hail taxis on the street you risk being scammed for high fares. There have also been occasional reports of taxi drivers sexually harassing single female passengers. You can download the GG taxi app on your phone when you arrive. GG is considered a reputable taxi app service in Armenia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public transport is often overcrowded, particularly in Yerevan. Yerevan buses are modern, but local buses in the regions may be old and poorly maintained."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel on the cross-border train service between Armenia and Georgia, secure your valuables, do not leave the compartment unattended, and lock the door from the inside."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Armenia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Armenia guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/armenia"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both a ",["1968 International Driving Permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence to drive in Armenia. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of driving is poor. Be prepared for drivers who drive recklessly and ignore traffic laws. Roads are in a poor state, particularly in the coldest months, from November to February. If possible avoid driving outside of cities and towns in the dark because of the poor condition of the roads and lack of lighting."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are walking, be careful when crossing roads and use subways where available."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list"]," (ASL) lists all known airlines in Armenia that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the UK. Check ASL when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK has placed sanctions on Aeroflot, Rossiya Airlines and Ural Airlines, which operate out of Russia and fly to Armenia. It is illegal under UK law for any British national or British company to buy tickets from these airlines."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of earthquakes. The last serious earthquake was in 1988 in the Lori region in the north. It killed between 25,000 and 50,000 people, injured thousands and left several cities in ruins."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Armenia. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Armenia-Azerbaijan border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border with Azerbaijan remains closed. FCDO advises against all travel to within 5km of the entire eastern border between Armenia and Azerbaijan. This is due to tensions between the 2 countries as a result of the conflict. Consular support is severely limited within this area."]},{"k":"h","s":["M16/H26 road between Ijevan and Noyemberyan"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel along the M16/H26 road between the towns of Ijevan and Noyemberyan. This is due to tensions between Armenia and Azerbaijan as a result of the conflict."]},{"k":"h","s":["Armenia-Turkey border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The land border with Turkey is closed, although there are scheduled direct flights between Yerevan and Istanbul."]},{"k":"h","s":["South Caucasus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travelling in the South Caucasus can be unpredictable and infrastructure is sometimes in a poor state of repair. Plan your travel carefully."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance with an English speaker."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Armenia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/12/armenia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Armenia, including Mount Aragats (4,090m elevation) and the lakes of Aragats (approximately 3,000m). Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare facilities in Armenia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public medical facilities and treatment in Yerevan are generally sufficient for minor or straightforward ailments. Public healthcare outside Yerevan is likely to be basic. Private hospitals in Armenia are of a good standard but can be expensive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Armenia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/armenia-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Armenia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Armenia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Armenia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Armenia"]," in Armenia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Armenia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/armenia-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Armenia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/armenia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]," such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/armenia/british-embassy-yerevan"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Armenia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-for-armenia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":14373,"change":"New information about entering Armenia across the land border from Iran (‘Entry requirements’ page)"},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/senegal":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"0c43b8795d864892a74f939b98450cdcc50014f87a775d3c01f3ca8d74e1c442","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/senegal","bytes":63060,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Senegal travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-26T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-15T10:00:14+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/senegal/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Senegal’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Senegal set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Embassy of Senegal in the UK","https://senegal-embassy.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Senegal, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Senegal without a visa for up to 3 months."]},{"k":"p","s":["You need to show border officials evidence of return or onward travel and proof of your arranged accommodation. If you do not have these, you may be refused entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to stay longer than 3 months, you must register with local authorities after you arrive. They will issue you with a ",["Carte d’étranger","https://interieur.sec.gouv.sn/services-aux-usagers/carte-didentite-detranger"],", which you must carry as identification."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re arriving from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],". This includes if you have transited through the airport of a country with risk of yellow fever transmission. Babies aged 9 months and under are exempt."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need a yellow fever certificate for onward travel to some other countries, due to the risk of yellow fever in Senegal."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about health entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Senegal guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/192/senegal#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Senegal","https://www.douanes.sn/ndn69/"]," (in French). You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Senegal","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/senegal/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Senegal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Senegal cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Several terrorist groups operate in neighbouring Mali, including Jama’a Nusrat ul-Islam wa al-Muslimin (JNIM) and Islamic State Sahel Province (ISSP). Whilst the regions most affected by terrorist activity are central and northern Mali, JNIM has increasingly conducted attacks in southern and western Mali near to the Senegalese border."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a threat of kidnapping in the wider Sahel region, which incorporates Mali, Mauritania, Niger, Chad and Burkina Faso, so take precautions to reduce the risk of kidnap in remote regions and border areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent demonstrations about political issues in Dakar and other cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations can turn violent. Protestors sometimes block major roads, including the road between Blaise Diagne International Airport and the city of Dakar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local media and ask local contacts about possible upcoming protests. Ahead of big demonstrations, if you’re in Dakar or another major city, consider stocking up on food, water and fuel. Once they have begun, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["continue to monitor local media for information"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the instructions of local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas where demonstrations are taking place and exercise caution"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in doubt about where protests are taking place, or the level of safety of an area, stay at home or in your hotel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals have been prosecuted for attending protests that have not been approved by the government."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cases of robbery, burglary and assault have become more common in Dakar, and in some cases, involve the use of weapons. Hotels frequented by foreign nationals have been targeted and robbed at gunpoint. Street crime like pickpocketing and bag-snatching is also on the increase in Dakar. To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying large sums of money or valuables"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a hotel safe to store passport and valuables whenever possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["be alert when withdrawing cash from ATMs, and where possible go by pre-arranged transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["be particularly careful after nightfall and avoid walking alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care of your belongings when arriving at and leaving hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep a copy of your passport’s photo page and your visa or entry stamp in a separate place"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bogus taxis at the airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of bogus taxi drivers pretending to know you and then overcharging you for the journey from the airport. Pre-arrange transport with your accommodation or an authorised operator. If you’re expecting someone to collect you at the airport, make sure they show you their ID."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fake currency"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious when changing cash, as there is a risk you will be scammed with fake money. Use ATMs or reputable exchange bureaux."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Senegal is a predominantly Muslim country. Dress and behave modestly in public, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or if you visit religious areas. In the main tourist areas there is more acceptance of western-style holiday clothing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bars and restaurants usually serve alcoholic drinks but drunkenness is considered offensive and penalties for drink-driving are severe."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kissing as a greeting is acceptable, but kissing romantically in public is not."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, do not drink alcohol or wear revealing clothes in public during Friday prayers between 1pm and 3pm."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the late afternoon and early evening when traffic will also be heavier than usual"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for possession, use or trafficking of illegal drugs. People accused regularly spend lengthy periods on remand before being tried. The maximum sentence for trafficking is 20 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prison conditions in Senegal are considerably poorer than in UK prisons. There may be problems such as overcrowding, lack of adequate meals, clean drinking water and electricity, and poor sanitation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only use reputable exchange bureaux to change your money. Dakar has ATMs that accept foreign bank cards, but there are few ATMs or bank facilities in the rest of the country. Withdrawal limits can be low, and ATMs regularly run out of money, including in Dakar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Larger or more upmarket establishments that cater for tourists usually accept foreign credit cards. Mobile payment applications, such as Orange Money and Wave, are also widely used around the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual acts are illegal in Senegal. The law is enforced and has led to arrests."]},{"k":"p","s":["On 30 March 2026, Senegal amended legislation increasing prison sentences for same-sex relations to 5–10 years and criminalise the “promotion, support or funding” of homosexuality, bisexuality and transsexuality."]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are generally not tolerated in Senegalese society. There is a risk of discrimination or harassment against individuals thought to be part of the LGBT+ community or perceived to be supporting their rights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Senegal, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Senegal with a UK driving licence for up to 6 months. A ",["1968 international driving permit","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," may be helpful in offering a translation for traffic officials. If you’re staying longer or living in Senegal, you must get a Senegalese driving licence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most main roads are of good quality, but minor roads can be in very poor repair. During the rainy season from June to September, torrential rains can cause floods and landslides which damage roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are not the same as in the UK. Drivers can make sudden movements without signalling and speeding is common. Many taxis and public mini-buses (‘cars rapides’) are not roadworthy by UK standards. Driving after dark is more dangerous because of poorly lit roads and vehicles without lights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic congestion gets worse in the run-up to and during religious festivals."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have an accident, you must contact the police on 17 and wait for them to arrive at the scene. Do not move your car until a police officer gives you permission. In remote areas, go to the nearest police station to report the accident."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Senegal. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/senegal"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/senegal/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Northern and eastern border areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care in remote areas of Senegal near the border areas with Mauritania and Mali."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist groups, including Jama’a Nusrat ul-Islam wa al-Muslimin (JNIM), are active in neighbouring Mali, and have carried out deadly attacks close to the border with Senegal. Border areas may be at risk or destabilised as the borders are not tightly controlled. See ",["‘Terrorism’","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/senegal/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Casamance Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["Casamance, the spur of land south of The Gambia, has suffered from decades of low-intensity separatist violence, largely directed at Senegalese security forces. Be on alert for clashes if you are travelling in the region, particularly close to the Gambian and Guinea-Bissauan borders. The risk of clashes is lower in the main tourist areas of the Casamance."]},{"k":"p","s":["When driving:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid travelling at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["stick to main roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel in convoy if possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not pull over if anyone tries flag you down"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that many roads in the Casamance are of low quality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Senegalese forces carry out minor operations near the border with The Gambia to combat wood trafficking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 15 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Senegal","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/192/senegal#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Senegal","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/192/senegal"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["diphtheria"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll find pharmacies which accept UK prescriptions in major cities. The NHS has information on ",["whether you can take your medicine abroad","https://www.nhs.uk/common-health-questions/medicines/can-i-take-my-medicine-abroad/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Senegal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in Dakar are reasonable, but are limited in the rest of Senegal. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Senegal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-recommemded-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Senegal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 15"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 18"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 17"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 123 for the military police, who may be more responsive if you are in the countryside."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=senegal"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=senegal"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=senegal"]," in Senegal"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Senegal","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/when-someone-dies-in-senegal"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Senegal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/senegal-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/senegal/british-embassy-dakar"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/senegal/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Senegal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-senegal"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":15593,"change":"Updated information about health risks you'll face in Senegal ('Health' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/samoa":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"eabc78d3ae0128e73de24d60919247801b54f733ad559babc26967aff511639e","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/samoa","bytes":42824,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Samoa travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2012-12-17T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-19T14:02:53+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/samoa/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Samoa’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Samoa set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Samoan High Commission in Brussels","https://samoaembassybelgium.com/visa-consular-services/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Samoa, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive. Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Samoa without a visa for up to 60 days. Border officials will issue a free visitor permit or business visitor permit using your arrival card. You may need to show:"]},{"k":"li","s":["an onward or return ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["sufficient funds – a bank statement is acceptable evidence"]},{"k":"li","s":["confirmed accommodation such as a hotel booking or letter of invitation"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer than 60 days, or for work, study or other reasons, ",["apply for a Samoan entry permit","https://mpmc.gov.ws/divisions/immigration/permits-2/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Samoa, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Samoa guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/188/samoa#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Departure tax for flights to American Samoa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are flying from Samoa to American Samoa, you must pay a departure tax of 40 Samoan tala."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict regulations covering the import of firearms, plant and animal products, pets and recreational drugs. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Samoa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 20,000 talas or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it with you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Samoa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Samoa, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["The level of serious crime is low, and incidents of petty theft are uncommon and opportunistic."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not leave your belongings unattended. Use hotel safes or deposit boxes for passports and valuables."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Local communities expect you to dress modestly when visiting towns and villages. Swimwear is acceptable on the beach or by streams and waterfalls, but anywhere else it is likely to receive negative attention."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mobile phone coverage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Phone coverage in rural areas and outlying islands can be limited or non-existent. Many UK mobile phones do not work, as your provider may not have an international roaming agreement in Samoa."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can buy Vodafone and Digicel SIM cards at the airport and at convenience stores and supermarkets. You must register your SIM card if you buy it locally."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink alcohol in public except at bars or restaurants. The legal drinking age is 21."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession of illegal drugs carries a possible 14-year prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Samoa and same-sex marriage is not recognised. Showing affection in public is likely to receive negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming and surfing safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Samoa’s tides can produce powerful currents in ocean lagoons. Take local advice before swimming. There have been fatal accidents at popular beaches."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many waves break directly on to reefs and the currents can be harsh. Take local advice before surfing."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more advice, see ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dive companies and tour operators may have limited resources and do not always observe safety and maintenance standards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check that your travel insurance covers you and see if the policy has conditions – for example, using a qualified instructor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ask the dive operator about the safety procedures they use. If you’re not satisfied, use a different provider."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Stray dogs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stray dogs are common in Apia and in many villages. They can become aggressive if you approach them or if they feel threatened. There have been cases of attacks by dogs. Keep your distance when cycling or walking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Samoa, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["To drive in Samoa, you must buy a temporary driving permit, which requires your UK driving licence. Car rental companies will help you with this. You can use the permit for up to 90 days a year. To drive for a longer period, you must get a Samoan driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The speed limit is 40kmph in towns and villages and 56kmph outside. If you have an accident, you must report it to the police within 24 hours. When driving near villages watch for children and animals on the roads. Avoid driving at night as roads are poorly lit and any hazards make driving very dangerous."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes and tsunamis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Samoa is part of the Pacific Ring of Fire, an active zone where earthquakes and tremors are a constant risk. The last major earthquake was in 2009."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"]," and resulting ",["tsunamis","https://www.ready.gov/tsunamis"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["The tropical cyclone season normally runs from November to the end of April, but most rain falls from December to March. Higher rainfall inland can cause flooding. Monitor local and international weather updates from the ",["World Meteorological Organization","https://severeweather.wmo.int/"],", the Samoa Meteorology Division or the Fiji Meteorological Service."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Samoa","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/188/samoa#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Samoa","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/188/samoa"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue take ",["precautions against being bitten by mosquitos","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/38/insect-and-tick-bite-avoidance"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Samoa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a medical emergency, evacuation to Australia, New Zealand or Hawaii is likely to be the only option for treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Samoa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["English-speaking lawyers in Samoa","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Samoa"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/samoa/british-high-commission-apia"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/samoa/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":10894,"change":"Updated information about global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/the-number-of-ndis-plan-managers-is-being-slashed-heres-what-we-know-so-far-297049":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-22T20:08Z","sha":"a4acb2e82634c56f4584ddd77290a677a938599e6117053849c34c691f425fa5","read":"https://theconversation.com/the-number-of-ndis-plan-managers-is-being-slashed-heres-what-we-know-so-far-297049","bytes":179775,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"The number of NDIS plan managers is being slashed. Here’s what we know so far","by":[{"n":"Mona Nikidehaghani","r":"Senior Lecturer in Accounting, University of Wollongong"}],"pub":"2026-11-22T18:38:13Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The federal government has ",["announced major changes","https://www.ndis.gov.au/changes-ndis/changes-plan-management"]," to how National Disability Insurance Scheme (NDIS) plans are managed."]},{"k":"p","s":["The aim is to reduce costs, tackle fraud and improve accountability."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under the new arrangements, participants who use plan management services will need to choose their plan manager from a government-approved panel of a limited number of providers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The number of plan managers – whether individuals or companies providing this service – could fall ",["from 1,442","https://www.health.gov.au/ministers/senator-the-hon-jenny-mcallister/media/work-starts-on-commissioning-ndis-plan-management-services"]," to ",["around 20","https://www.smh.com.au/politics/federal/the-next-big-ndis-cut-plan-managers-to-be-slashed-from-1442-to-20-in-fraud-crackdown-20261118-p61f6u.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Here’s what this change means for people with disability."]},{"k":"h","s":["Who or what are NDIS plan managers?"]},{"k":"p","s":["NDIS participants have ",["three main options","https://www.ndis.gov.au/participants/using-your-funding/plan-implementation-meeting/guide-your-management-options"]," for managing their funding. They can manage it themselves, have the National Disability Insurance Agency (NDIA) manage it, or engage a registered plan manager. They can also combine these options."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Plan managers","https://www.ndis.gov.au/participants/working-providers/support-coordinators-and-plan-managers/what-plan-manager"]," help participants manage the financial and administrative aspects of their NDIS funding. They check invoices, submit NDIS claims, pay service providers, keep financial records and help participants track their spending."]},{"k":"p","s":["Until recently, individuals and businesses could become plan managers by meeting NDIS registration requirements. According to ",["NDIS data","https://www.ndis.gov.au/providers/pricing-and-payments/pricing/pricing-updates"],", companies account for around 75% of active plan management providers."]},{"k":"p","s":["For many people with disability and their families, navigating the NDIS can be complex and time-consuming. Using a plan manager reduces this administrative burden. It gives participants greater flexibility in choosing services that meet their needs."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NDIS provides separate funding for plan management services."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is a popular option. According to the NDIA’s ",["June 2026 quarterly report","https://www.ndis.gov.au/publications/quarterly-reports/archived-quarterly-reports-2025-26"],", 64% of NDIS participants used plan managers, who handled A$8.6 billion in payments in just three months."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why is the government concerned?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The government has raised significant ",["concerns","https://www.ndiscommission.gov.au/provider-registration/about-registration/changes-registration-plan-management-services"]," about the integrity of the plan management system."]},{"k":"p","s":["Between July and September 2026, ",["the NDIA rejected","https://www.health.gov.au/ministers/senator-the-hon-jenny-mcallister/media/work-starts-on-commissioning-ndis-plan-management-services"]," more than 3,500 claims submitted through plan managers, worth more than $5.8 million."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 40% of cases, they had authorised payments for services that hadn’t been delivered."]},{"k":"p","s":["Almost 1,000 plan managers are currently subject to ",["additional checks","https://www.health.gov.au/ministers/senator-the-hon-jenny-mcallister/media/work-starts-on-commissioning-ndis-plan-management-services"]," because of concerns about how funds are being used or non-compliance with NDIS requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, being subject to additional checks does not necessarily mean a plan manager has committed fraud."]},{"k":"p","s":["Conflicts of interest are ",["another concern","https://www.ndis.gov.au/news/11769-work-starts-commissioning-ndis-plan-management-services"],". For example, plan managers may refer participants to disability service providers with which they have commercial relationships."]},{"k":"h","s":["What is changing?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Under the new arrangements, the existing open market of registered plan managers will be replaced by a government-approved panel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only a limited number of providers will be chosen to join the panel through a competitive process to start in ",["April 2027","https://www.health.gov.au/ministers/senator-the-hon-jenny-mcallister/media/work-starts-on-commissioning-ndis-plan-management-services"],". The panel will commence from ",["October 2027","https://www.ndis.gov.au/changes-ndis/changes-plan-management"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Participants who use plan management services will be required to choose a provider from this panel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Those whose existing plan managers are not on the panel will need to move to an approved provider ",["within six months","https://www.ndis.gov.au/changes-ndis/changes-plan-management"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, the NDIS Quality and Safeguards Commission has ",["suspended most new registration applications","https://www.ndiscommission.gov.au/provider-registration/about-registration/changes-registration-plan-management-services"]," for plan management services."]},{"k":"h","s":["What are the potential benefits?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Having fewer plan managers could make it easier for the government to monitor spending, enforce consistent standards and identify fraudulent claims."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stronger financial controls could also protect participants from unauthorised spending and prevent their funding from being used for services they have not received."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, whether these changes deliver better outcomes for participants will depend on how they are implemented."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["With NDIS changes set to pass, here’s who bears the cost of making it ‘sustainable’","https://theconversation.com/with-ndis-changes-set-to-pass-heres-who-bears-the-cost-of-making-it-sustainable-285372"]]},{"k":"h","s":["What are the potential risks?"]},{"k":"p","s":["For some participants, the relationship with their plan manager goes well beyond processing invoices."]},{"k":"p","s":["They may have worked with the same plan manager for years and have developed a trusting relationship. Their plan manager will have developed an understanding of their individual circumstances, needs and the challenges they face in navigating the NDIS."]},{"k":"p","s":["Losing these relationships could be particularly difficult for some people with disability."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are also practical questions. How will participants find a new plan manager? How will they know which provider best meets their needs? Who will help those who struggle to navigate the system independently?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Capacity is another concern if the number of businesses permitted to work as plan managers is limited to just 20. Will the selected providers have sufficient staff, technology and resources to accommodate a potentially large influx of participants without compromising service quality?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Changing plan managers also involves transferring financial records, establishing new service arrangements and dealing with outstanding invoices."]},{"k":"p","s":["If these processes are not managed effectively, participants could face delays in using their NDIS funding. Service providers could also face delays in receiving payments."]},{"k":"p","s":["This could particularly affect smaller service providers that rely on timely payments to pay their staff and continue operating."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is also unclear how plan managers will be chosen for the panel. What criteria will the government use to assess providers? Will artificial intelligence (AI) or other automated technologies be used in the selection process? How will the process ensure managers are selected based on their ability to meet participants’ diverse needs, rather than mainly on financial criteria?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Confused about the NDIS changes? Here’s what’s coming, and what’s still being worked out","https://theconversation.com/confused-about-the-ndis-changes-heres-whats-coming-and-whats-still-being-worked-out-290138"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting the balance right"]},{"k":"p","s":["Strengthening financial accountability and tackling fraud are necessary to protect both taxpayers and people with disability."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, reducing the number of plan managers does not automatically guarantee better services or stronger accountability."]},{"k":"p","s":["The success of these reforms should be measured by more than financial savings. It should consider whether they improve the experiences of people with disability, protect their choice and control, reduce administrative burdens and support their independence and wellbeing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rushing the transition could create new problems for the very people the reforms are intended to protect."]}],"chars":6287},"https://theconversation.com/10-years-after-nzs-7-8-earthquake-a-changed-coastline-offers-clues-to-future-hazards-297266":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-24T21:39Z","sha":"9845237042d03aa0a785ee3f3f6d6a2d4739e2e7a27c400e60b2b72242493d79","read":"https://theconversation.com/10-years-after-nzs-7-8-earthquake-a-changed-coastline-offers-clues-to-future-hazards-297266","bytes":185082,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"10 years after NZ’s 7.8 earthquake, a changed coastline offers clues to future hazards","by":[{"n":"Wayne Stephenson","r":"Professor of Geography, University of Otago"},{"n":"Mark Dickson","r":"Professor, School of Environment, University of Auckland, Waipapa Taumata Rau"}],"pub":"2026-11-24T20:34:52Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Ten years ago this month, ",["the magnitude 7.8 Kaikōura earthquake","https://www.geonet.org.nz/earthquake/story/2016p858000"]," suddenly transformed landscapes across New Zealand’s upper South Island."]},{"k":"p","s":["One of the most dramatic changes occurred along the Kaikōura Peninsula, where ",["stretches of rocky coastline","https://earthjay.com/earthquakes/20161114_New_Nealand/Coastal%20Uplift_%20How%20has%20the%20Kaikoura%20Coastline%20Changed%20-%20Earthquake%20-%20GeoNet.html"]," were lifted above the tides."]},{"k":"p","s":["By chance, scientists had already been measuring erosion along the peninsula’s rocky shores for more than four decades, giving them a rare opportunity to compare how quickly the coastline was wearing away before and after the earthquake."]},{"k":"p","s":["Now, drawing on more than 50 years of measurements, ",["our new research","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/esp.70360"]," shows that erosion rates more than doubled following the earthquake’s abrupt uplift."]},{"k":"p","s":["The findings also suggest that erosion can erase evidence of earlier earthquakes much faster than previously assumed – potentially leaving gaps in the geological record used to estimate future earthquake hazards."]},{"k":"h","s":["Half a century of coastal research"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cliffs and shore platforms ",["are common on New Zealand’s coasts","https://teara.govt.nz/en/coastal-shoreline/print"],". These platforms are wide, relatively flat rock surfaces at the base of cliffs that become exposed at low tide."]},{"k":"p","s":["They provide important habitats for marine life and a natural playground for families exploring rock pools. Rock coasts might appear relatively permanent, but they are continually eroded and weathered by waves, water, salt and animals such as limpets."]},{"k":"p","s":["Geomorphologists study how these processes erode bedrock and shape coastlines. Shore platforms also provide evidence of changes in sea level and shoreline position caused by earthquakes."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 1973, pioneering coastal geomorphologist ",["Bob Kirk","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/nzg.12041_2"]," of the University of Canterbury began measuring erosion on Kaikōura Peninsula’s shore platforms. Kirk, ",["who died in 2024","https://www.thepress.co.nz/nz-news/350262067/life-story-passionate-geographer-academic-leader-and-regional-councillor"],", used an innovative instrument called a ",["micro-erosion meter","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0012825209000543"],", which allowed him to measure precisely how quickly the rock surfaces were wearing away."]},{"k":"p","s":[["His results","https://rsnz.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1080/00288306.1977.10427603"],", published in 1977, showed that, on average, the platforms were lowered by about 1.5 mm per year. This might not seem much on human timescales, but over several thousand years it adds up."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 1993, the monitoring network was expanded, and measurements have continued over subsequent decades. By 2016, the network had provided 43 years of data, showing an average erosion rate of about 1 mm per year, slightly less than Kirk’s original number."]},{"k":"p","s":["We attribute this difference to the longer record and the loss of some very fast-eroding sites. Despite this, erosion rates remained broadly consistent before the earthquake."]},{"k":"h","s":["How an earthquake changed the coastline"]},{"k":"p","s":["On November 14 2016, the Kaikōura earthquake ",["lifted the peninsula","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0012821X17303722?via%3Dihub"]," by about a metre, raising parts of the shore platforms above the tide and creating a landform we call a ",["marine terrace","https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/earth-and-planetary-sciences/marine-terrace"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["These terraces can be found around New Zealand’s coast and in other countries where tectonic processes cause uplift. Sequences of marine terraces resemble steps, each representing an episode of uplift."]},{"k":"p","s":["Using dating techniques, geologists can reconstruct the timing of past earthquakes from the age, number and heights of these terraces, and use evidence of uplift to help estimate their magnitude."]},{"k":"p","s":["But there’s a complication. If the uplift is about the same as the tidal range, the edge of the new marine terrace can remain connected to a shore platform still exposed to the tides."]},{"k":"p","s":["Erosion then continues to wear down the platform and eat back into the terrace. For the terrace to survive as evidence of the earthquake, another uplift event must raise it beyond the reach of the sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["So, how long does it take for erosion to remove a newly formed marine terrace? Since 2016, we have measured the monitoring network 27 times. In 2024, we passed the 50-year milestone, making Kaikōura the world’s longest-running record of shore platform erosion."]},{"k":"p","s":["Overall, we found erosion rates more than doubled after the earthquake, to around 2.5mm per year."]},{"k":"p","s":["The uplift exposed rock surfaces to different weathering processes, including drying, temperature changes and salt crystallisation. Mudstone surfaces were particularly vulnerable, eroding more than twice as fast as limestone."]},{"k":"p","s":["We used the new erosion rate to predict how long it would take for the metre-high marine terrace to disappear."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, erosion is expected to slow over time. Accounting for this, we calculated that the new terrace could disappear within about 550 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["But other processes are important. One is ",["sea-level rise","https://www.gns.cri.nz/our-science/environment-and-climate/coastal-change/sea-level-rise/"],". Another is a quirk of geology: despite the sudden uplift, Kaikōura Peninsula gradually subsides between earthquakes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Adding this subsidence and sea-level rise to the calculation reduces the estimated time to just 200 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["That gives us a window of 200–550 years, shorter than the estimated time between major earthquakes capable of creating these terraces. It’s therefore probable that the new terrace will disappear before another earthquake can preserve it."]},{"k":"h","s":["What disappearing terraces mean for earthquake records"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our findings show that a marine terrace can be eroded away before the next earthquake."]},{"k":"p","s":["If one or more terraces have disappeared from a site, we may unknowingly underestimate how frequently large earthquakes occurred in the past."]},{"k":"p","s":["We may also overestimate their magnitude if the uplift produced by several earthquakes is mistakenly attributed to a single event."]},{"k":"p","s":["This could affect ",["seismic hazard models","https://www.gns.cri.nz/research-projects/national-seismic-hazard-model/"],", which rely partly on geological evidence to estimate the likelihood of future earthquakes."]},{"k":"p","s":["More than 50 years after Bob Kirk first asked how quickly shore platforms erode, our measurements are helping us answer a much bigger question: how complete are marine terrace records of earthquakes?"]}],"chars":5561},"https://theconversation.com/setahun-pascabencana-sumatra-pemulihan-belum-tuntas-banjir-kembali-menghantam-295967":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-28T04:52Z","sha":"b9216d5279570b11be7dcf37a58823db4da727853e2724e1b710dbf1d0f8daf5","read":"https://theconversation.com/setahun-pascabencana-sumatra-pemulihan-belum-tuntas-banjir-kembali-menghantam-295967","bytes":185280,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Setahun pascabencana Sumatra: Pemulihan belum tuntas, banjir kembali menghantam","by":[{"n":"Resti Pujihasvuty","r":"Researcher at Family Dynamic Research Group; Research Center for Population, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"},{"n":"Achmat Sarifudin","r":"Peneliti Utama, Pusat Riset Teknologi Proses, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"},{"n":"Nirma Yossa","r":"Peneliti Pusat Riset Kependudukan, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"},{"n":"Rahmat Saleh","r":"Peneliti, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"},{"n":"Siti Khudaifany","r":"Teknisi Litkayasa, Direktorat Pengelolaan Laboratorium Fasilitas Riset dan Kawasan Sains dan Teknologi, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"},{"n":"Yanu Endar Prasetyo","r":"Researcher at Research Center for Population - BRIN, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"}],"pub":"2026-11-28T04:01:46Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["● Setahun pascabencana, infrastruktur pulih, tetapi hunian dan penghidupan warga tertinggal."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Perempuan menopang keluarga melalui kerja perawatan dan usaha kecil pascabencana."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Pemulihan harus adil, berkelanjutan, dan tidak membebani perempuan sendirian."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Malam itu, pada bulan yang sama tahun lalu, hujan turun tanpa henti sejak petang","https://futuremovement.id/catatan-lapangan-13-perempuan-perempuan-tangguh-dayah-husen/"],". Sekitar pukul dua dini hari, air bah bercampur kayu gelondongan menerjang Gampong Dayah Usen di Kecamatan Meurah Dua, Pidie Jaya, Aceh."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seorang ibu terjepit atap seng dan batang kayu di bawah pohon belimbing. Ia baru bisa dievakuasi lima hari kemudian, dengan keranda."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hampir setahun berselang, air kembali datang. Banjir yang mulai merendam Pidie Jaya pada malam 8 November 2026 ",["berdampak pada 32.272 jiwa","https://www.metrotvnews.com/read/koGCgYyg-banjir-rendam-pidie-jaya-32-272-jiwa-terdampak"],". Beberapa keluarga dari Gampong Dayah Usen kembali mengungsi ke meunasah (bangunan yang berada di tempat lebih tinggi)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Saat bencana, meunasah ",["menjadi penanda bagi warga:","https://futuremovement.id/catatan-lapangan-14-meunasah-sebagai-ruang-pemulihan-pascabencana/"]," selama air belum menyentuh meunasah, mereka akan tetap bertahan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada 26 November 2026, genap setahun banjir bandang dan longsor yang ",["menewaskan 1.024 orang di Aceh","https://theconversation.com/korban-bencana-sumatra-menyambut-lebaran-dengan-cemas-imbas-pemulihan-belum-efektif-277434"],", Sumatera Utara, dan Sumatera Barat. Selama setahun ini, perhatian publik tertuju pada pembangunan fisik: rumah, jembatan, dan jalan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, sudahkah warga benar-benar pulih? Apa yang sudah pulih, dan apa yang masih tertinggal?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Sudah pulihkah?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Di atas kertas, capaian pemerintah terlihat menenangkan. Pemerintah melaporkan progres rehabilitasi dan rekonstruksi di tiga provinsi mencapai 96–98%, meski angka itu hanya mengacu pada kegiatan ",["tahun anggaran 2026","https://www.kemenkopmk.go.id/menko-pmk-11-bulan-pascabencana-sumatra-pemerintah-pastikan-pemulihan-berjalan-sesuai-rencana"],", bukan keseluruhan proses pemulihan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Bukan sekadar krisis alam, Banjir Sumatra mencerminkan krisis pendanaan","https://theconversation.com/bukan-sekadar-krisis-alam-banjir-sumatra-mencerminkan-krisis-pendanaan-272324"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Data Satuan Tugas Percepatan Rehabilitasi dan Rekonstruksi (PRR) di Aceh per 18 November 2026 menunjukkan capaian yang timpang. Sekitar ",["94% ruas","https://www.infoaceh.net/2026/11/20/setahun-pascabencana-huntap-baru-357-persen-rekonstruksi-aceh-rp5897-triliun-berlanjut-hingga-2028/"]," jalan daerah sudah berfungsi. Namun, dari 49.184 hunian tetap yang direncanakan, baru 1.758 unit atau 3,57% yang rampung. Rekonstruksi Aceh senilai hampir Rp59 triliun bahkan baru ditargetkan selesai pada 2028."]},{"k":"p","s":["Koalisi masyarakat sipil pun menilai ",["pemulihan masih lamban","https://rri.co.id/nasional/2905779/pemerhati-nilai-pemulihan-sumatra-belum-tuntas-setahun-pascabencana"],", terutama untuk sawah dan kebun warga. Per Agustus 2026, sekitar ",["259 hektare sawah yang rusak","https://nu.or.id/daerah/masa-transisi-pascabencana-diperpanjang-hingga-akhir-2026-pcnu-pidie-jaya-dorong-percepatan-pemulihan-masyarakat-AxnUv"]," berat di Pidie Jaya baru diusulkan untuk ditangani pada 2027."]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalan pemulihan juga semakin kompleks karena sejumlah daerah kembali dilanda bencana sepanjang 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada November saja, banjir dan longsor melanda berbagai wilayah, termasuk ",["Aceh, Sumatera Utara, Sumatera Barat, Jawa Barat, Jawa Tengah, dan Kalimantan Barat","https://bnpb.go.id/berita/perkembangan-situasi-dan-penanganan-bencana-di-tanah-air-27-november-2026"],". Di Aceh, banjir kembali berdampak pada Subulussalam dan Aceh Singkil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Situasi ini menunjukkan bahwa pemulihan pascabencana bukan berlangsung dalam kondisi yang stabil. Ketika warga masih berusaha membangun kembali rumah, mata pencaharian, dan kehidupan mereka setelah bencana sebelumnya, bencana baru kembali mengancam dan menambah beban pemulihan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Perempuan menopang dalam diam"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika penghasilan hilang, kebutuhan tidak ikut berhenti. Di masa paling sulit, perempuan menjadi penopang keluarga. Para ibu menjual melinjo dan pinang yang tersisa untuk membeli gas atau susu bayi."]},{"k":"p","s":["“Anak-anak tidak mengerti musibah. Yang mereka tahu cuma minta uang jajan,” ",["tutur seorang ibu","https://futuremovement.id/catatan-lapangan-13-perempuan-perempuan-tangguh-dayah-husen/"],". Jadi, mamanya yang berputar otak.“"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Di setiap bencana, perempuan selalu menanggung beban ganda","https://theconversation.com/di-setiap-bencana-perempuan-selalu-menanggung-beban-ganda-272588"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Aceh Tamiang, seorang perempuan muda pembuat kue kehilangan seluruh peralatan produksi dan bahan baku saat banjir bandang. Setelah mendapat bantuan sarana produksi, ia kembali berproduksi dan meraup omzet sekitar ",["Rp10,1 juta","https://ejurnalunsam.id/index.php/mardika/article/view/15373"]," selama Ramadhan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di sela itu, perempuan tetap merawat anak, lansia, dan anggota keluarga yang sakit. Kerja perawatan tak berbayar (unpaid care work) ini jarang tercatat dalam laporan resmi, padahal menjadi penyangga keluarga. Di Asia dan Pasifik, perempuan menanggung sekitar ",["80% jam kerja perawatan tak berbayar","https://www.ilo.org/resource/news/ilo-women-do-4-times-more-unpaid-care-work-men-asia-and-pacific"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Kajian tentang peran perempuan terdampak bencana di Aceh","https://www.atlantis-press.com/proceedings/irisecon-26/126026672"]," mencatat sekitar 68% program pemulihan penghidupan berbasis komunitas yang terdokumentasi di Aceh pascabencana digerakkan oleh inisiatif akar rumput perempuan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, modal yang terbatas, pasar yang belum stabil, dan banjir berulang bisa menghentikan produksi kapan saja. Para ibu di Dayah Usen berharap bantuan ",["tidak berhenti","https://futuremovement.id/catatan-lapangan-13-perempuan-perempuan-tangguh-dayah-husen/"]," pada uang tunai dan sembako, tetapi juga mencakup pendampingan usaha."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sementara itu, bantuan pemerintah untuk usaha kecil di Aceh tahun ini senilai Rp2,6 miliar, sebagian besar ",["berupa mesin produksi","https://investortrust.id/macro/121515/pulihkan-ekonomi-pascabencana-di-aceh-kementerian-umkm-gelontorkan-rp-2-6-miliar-untuk-alat-produksi"],". Usaha pangan rumahan yang banyak digeluti perempuan belum menjadi perhatian memadai."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pemberdayaan jangan menjadi beban baru"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketangguhan perempuan patut diapresiasi, tetapi tidak boleh menjadi alasan untuk membebankan pemulihan kepada mereka."]},{"k":"p","s":["Studi terbaru tentang ",["banjir di Pekalongan, Jawa Tengah","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/gwao.70216"]," menunjukkan perempuan cenderung mengalami gangguan penghidupan lebih lama dan lebih sulit mengakses sumber daya pemulihan. Jika pemulihan ekonomi hanya bertumpu pada perempuan, beban mereka akan makin berlapis."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Kajian tentang kritik terhadap program pengentasan kemiskinan","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00220380701789810"]," menemukan bahwa menjadikan perempuan sasaran utama justru menambah tanggung jawab mereka tanpa pembagian peran yang adil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Gampong Dayah Usen, ketegangan mulai terlihat. \"Janganlah ibu-ibu terus yang dibantu, kami juga mau,” ",["keluh perangkat desa","https://futuremovement.id/catatan-lapangan-11-tolong-jangan-lepas-kami/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Banyak bapak kehilangan alat kerja. Pemulihan yang hanya menyasar satu kelompok bisa memicu kecemburuan sosial, padahal laki-laki juga membutuhkan pemulihan penghidupan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Menatap tahun kedua upaya pemulihan"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Kajian pemulihan penghidupan pascatsunami Aceh 2004","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00074910902836171"]," sudah menekankan pentingnya memperhitungkan aset, peluang ekonomi, dan kebutuhan lokal. Semangat ",["build back better (membangun kembali lebih baik)","https://www.undrr.org/publication/sendai-framework-disaster-risk-reduction-2015-2030"]," seharusnya juga berlaku bagi ekonomi keluarga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Memasuki tahun kedua, pemerintah perlu membenahi tiga hal:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pertama, ubah ukuran keberhasilan pemulihan. ",["Selain rumah dan jalan","https://www.mdpi.com/2071-1050/15/24/16870"],", pemerintah perlu memantau apakah pendapatan keluarga pulih, lahan kembali digarap, dan warga mampu memenuhi kebutuhan tanpa terus menunggu bantuan. Data terpilah menurut jenis kelamin juga diperlukan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kedua, pemulihan penghidupan perlu dipandang sebagai proses jangka panjang. Dukungan bagi usaha warga perlu berkelanjutan hingga benar-benar mandiri dan memperhitungkan risiko bencana berulang. Kerja perempuan yang selama ini tak terlihat, termasuk kerja perawatan, juga harus diakui sebagai bagian dari pemulihan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketiga, terapkan pengarustamaan gender sejak perencanaan. Perspektif gender bukan berarti semua bantuan diarahkan kepada perempuan. Pemulihan harus memulihkan penghidupan laki-laki, melibatkan mereka dalam pengasuhan, dan membagi kerja rumah tangga secara adil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Musim hujan sudah tiba lagi. Bagi warga Aceh, khususnya Gampong Dayah Usen, meunasah kembali menjadi patokan. Namun, selama hujan masih memicu ketakutan, pemulihan belum selesai."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemulihan baru tuntas ketika keluarga kembali punya penghasilan, hujan tak lagi memicu kecemasan, dan beban untuk bangkit dipikul bersama—bukan oleh perempuan seorang diri."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Partisipasi dan keterlibatan perempuan Aceh perlu mendapat dukungan lebih","https://theconversation.com/partisipasi-dan-keterlibatan-perempuan-aceh-perlu-mendapat-dukungan-lebih-245569"]]}],"chars":6975}};
